INT. SNOWBOUND CABIN - DAY

Frost on the panes. A woodstove, nearly dead. Five survivors packed around a table with a single can between them.

CAPTAIN HENRIETTA "HETTY" MBATHA-FLORES, 50s, pilot, scrapes the last bean from the can.
DR. OSKAR LINDQVIST-AKINTOLA, 40s, holds a splinted arm to his chest.
JUNIPER "JUNE" ACHEBE-RYDER, 20s, shivers in an oversized parka.
TOMASZ BRZEZINSKI, 60s, glowers at the stove.
And little MIRABEL ODUYA-HART, 10, wrapped in a blanket, eyes huge.

HETTY
Fire's out in an hour.

OSKAR
We need wood.

TOMASZ
We need a plan.

JUNE
We need to stop shouting.

TOMASZ
Nobody's shouting.

HETTY
Tomasz, you are.

TOMASZ
I'm projecting.

OSKAR
At whom?

TOMASZ
At whoever gets us killed.

JUNE
Nobody's getting killed.

MIRABEL
Is Dad coming?

Silence. Hetty sets down the can. Oskar studies the floor.

HETTY
Mirabel, sweetheart. The radio's down.

MIRABEL
But they know where we are.

OSKAR
They know where the plane went down.

TOMASZ
Which is twelve miles west.

JUNE
We could walk.

OSKAR
She means him, in the blanket, with a broken arm. And her. And me.

TOMASZ
Then I go alone.

HETTY
You'll freeze.

TOMASZ
He'll freeze if I don't.

OSKAR
Who? Me?

TOMASZ
Both of you. All of you.

HETTY
Nobody goes alone.

JUNE
I'll go with him.

TOMASZ
She'll slow me.

HETTY
She'll keep you alive.

MIRABEL
I want to come.

HETTY
No, Mirabel.

MIRABEL
Why not?

OSKAR
Because she is the only reason the rest of us stay.

Mirabel looks from face to face. Tomasz rises and takes his coat from the hook.

TOMASZ
At dawn, then.

HETTY
At dawn.

JUNE
(quietly)
I'll get the rope.
